      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If a board has both `CONFIG_BATTERY_INIT_TYPE_RETRY_COUNT` and `CONFIG_BATTERY_INIT_TYPE_DEFERRED_RETRY_COUNT` configured, using `MAX` here will result in fewer total retries than before. \n\nPreviously, the code would do `CONFIG_BATTERY_INIT_TYPE_RETRY_COUNT` synchronous retries *per* deferred attempt, resulting in effectively `(1 + RETRY_COUNT) * (1 + DEFERRED_RETRY_COUNT)` total attempts. Now it\u0027s just `1 + MAX(RETRY_COUNT, DEFERRED_RETRY_COUNT)`.\n\nIf both configs aren\u0027t meant to be used together anyway, this is perfectly fine, but I wanted to point out the subtle change in behavior.",
